# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.17 slice 4 — G0: the post-rewrite grammar with NO guard.
#
# This is P5's transparent-holder shape (`.13` slice 5b) hand-eliminated at `prim`, PLUS the one
# ingredient every earlier synthetic in this family lacks: SystemVerilog's own LAYOUT MODEL — a
# nullable `trivia` rule leading every token. Slice 2 measured that layout fact as the second of the
# two causes of `exact = 0 of 157`, and no probe in this tree had ever carried it.
#
# THE MAPPING onto the shipped grammar, rule for rule:
#
#   scratch     := kw_k eq outer_cast semi      ~ the enclosing statement, which is what makes the
#                                                 holder MANDATORY. `initial k = 8'(1);` — without
#                                                 the trailing `;` the outer context is optional and
#                                                 the starvation hides behind a shorter parse.
#   outer_cast  := ct tick lparen lit rparen    ~ cast := casting_type tick lparen expression rparen
#                                                 THE HOLDER. Its residual after `ct` is
#                                                 `tick lparen lit rparen` — the byte set the guard
#                                                 would test, and the sub-parse the structural guard
#                                                 would run.
#   ct          := kw | prim                    ~ casting_type := simple_type | constant_primary
#                                                 TRANSPARENT to `prim` on its second arm, so the
#                                                 holder is one hop out (`guard_hops = 1`).
#   prim        := prim_base ( prim_suffix )*   ~ constant_primary := …_lr_base ( …_lr_suffix )*
#                                                 THE POSSESSIVE LOOP. `.17`'s entire subject.
#   prim_base   := lit | cast_seed              ~ the acyclic left corners plus the sheared clone
#   cast_seed   := kw tick lparen lit rparen    ~ constant_cast over a casting_type shorn of its
#                                                 constant_primary arm — `.13` slice 5's clone
#   prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen       ~ constant_cast's residual after its leading
#                                                 casting_type — what the `*` iterates
#
# ⛔ WHAT THIS FILE MUST DO: STARVE. It is the negative control for `g1_byte_guard.ebnf` and
# `g2_structural_guard.ebnf`, which differ from it by exactly one lookahead inside the `*` and
# nothing else. If G0 ever starts accepting E1, the bank is measuring something other than the
# starvation and every conclusion drawn from it is void.
#
# The entry rule is named `scratch` so this file loads into the scratch slot verbatim:
#   cp <this file> grammars/scratch/scratch.ebnf && make -C rust SHELL=/bin/bash focus_scratch
@entry: true
scratch := kw_k eq outer_cast semi
outer_cast := ct tick lparen lit rparen
ct := kw | prim
prim := prim_base ( prim_suffix )*
prim_base := lit | cast_seed
cast_seed := kw tick lparen lit rparen
prim_suffix := tick lparen lit rparen

# ---- the token tier. Every token begins with `trivia`, exactly as `grammars/systemverilog.ebnf`
# writes `tick := trivia "'"` (:7151), `lparen := trivia "("` (:7105), `rparen := trivia ")"` (:7130).
lit := trivia /n/
kw := trivia /t/
kw_k := trivia /k/
eq := trivia "="
semi := trivia ";"
tick := trivia "'"
lparen := trivia "("
rparen := trivia ")"

# ---- the layout tier, copied in shape from `grammars/systemverilog.ebnf:618-624`. NULLABLE, and it
# leads every token — which is precisely why `/` is in the FIRST set of every token and why a
# byte-set guard over FIRST(residual) cannot be exact anywhere on SystemVerilog.
@branch_policy: priority_first
trivia := (line_comment | block_comment)*
line_comment := /\/\/[^\n]*(\n|$)/
block_comment := /\/\*([^*]|\*+[^*\/])*\*+\//
